# =============================================================================
# Use It Fresh — what belongs in git
#
# The DSL is the source of truth: dsl/, supabase/migrations/, design/scripts/,
# docs/ and the typed SDK. Those are small, diff cleanly, and can rebuild the
# app. Everything below is either regenerated, enormous, or secret.
# =============================================================================

# --- secrets: never commit -----------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.p8
*.p12
*.keystore
*.jks
.flutterflow/.env

# --- regenerated on every push -------------------------------------------
# generated_code/ is the exported Flutter app. It is rewritten wholesale each
# time, so committing it means a 78MB diff per push and no readable history.
# The DSL that produces it IS committed, which is the part worth versioning.
generated_code/
.dart_tool/
.packages
build/
.ffai_staging/

# --- SDK + local run state ------------------------------------------------
.flutterflow/sdk/
.flutterflow/runs.jsonl
.flutterflow/history/
.flutterflow/traces/
.flutterflow/backups/
.flutterflow/support/
.flutterflow/workspace.json
.flutterflow/last_run.json
.flutterflow/recovery.json
.flutterflow/plan.md
.flutterflow/project_sdk_meta.json
.flutterflow/generated_code_state.json

# --- design binaries ------------------------------------------------------
# 62MB of source zips and render output. Git keeps every version of a binary
# forever, so these would permanently bloat the clone for everyone.
# design/scripts/ IS committed and can re-render the clips from source.
design/*.zip
design/*.mp4
design/*.png
design/*.jpg
design/*.webp

# Keep the render pipeline and the docs that explain it.
!design/scripts/**
!design/*.md

# The entrance frames ARE committed, unlike the rest of design/. They are not
# working files — they are the app's artwork, served straight from this repo
# through jsDelivr's CDN. FlutterFlow gives uploaded assets random URLs that
# cannot be derived, and there are 47 of them; committing here means the paths
# are predictable, the frames are versioned with the code that plays them, and
# nobody has to paste 47 links.
!design/entrance/**

# Same reasoning for the brand marks the app displays.
!design/brand/**

# The navigation icons the app displays, same reasoning again.
!design/nav/**

# The v2 screen guide is the design source of truth for the current rebuild —
# small enough to keep, and the reference every screen is being built against.
!design/Chat GPT/Use-It-Fresh-Screen-Guide-v2/**

# Visual direction v3: the six card photographs (resized for the app) and the
# approved logo. These are served to the app over jsDelivr, so they have to be
# committed; the PNG masters stay out.
!design/v3/**
!design/Chat GPT/Use-It-Fresh-Visual-v3/*.md
!design/Chat GPT/Use-It-Fresh-Visual-v3/tokens.json
!design/Chat GPT/Use-It-Fresh-Visual-v3/icons/**
!design/Chat GPT/Use-It-Fresh-Visual-v3/logo/**

# The kitchen icon set, served to the app over jsDelivr alongside the food
# photography. PNG at 256 so one file covers every size the guide asks for.
!design/v3/icons/**
!design/Chat GPT/Use-It-Fresh-Kitchen-Icons/**
